## 18. Passport format and export

Generate a professional downloadable PDF document if the existing project can support this safely and efficiently.

Use a suitable PDF library already installed, if available.

Avoid introducing a large dependency solely for document styling.

If PDF generation is impractical within the existing architecture, implement a structured printable document as a safe alternative and report the limitation.

The Passport should include:

- Professional layout.
- Clear section headings.
- TehlayPay branding.
- Readable typography.
- Clear PASS, BLOCKED and REVIEW indicators.
- Document reference.
- Page numbering where applicable.

The Passport must remain readable when printed.

Do not present a Passport as a legally certified procurement document or an independently verified third-party certificate.

It is a TehlayPay-generated procurement decision record.

## 19. Passport verification and integrity

The Passport should contain a unique reference that can be matched to its underlying audit record.

If the existing audit store supports integrity checksums or hashes, use the existing mechanism.

Do not invent a cryptographic verification system that is not implemented.

If feasible, provide a verification action within the application that retrieves the relevant stored record and confirms whether the Passport's reference corresponds to an existing audit record.

Clearly distinguish:
- Record exists.
- Record matches stored audit data.
- Payment capture was independently confirmed by PayPal.

Do not claim cryptographic authenticity unless the implementation actually verifies it.

Do not expose sensitive internal audit details publicly.

